//  470 /*************************************************************************************************
//  471  *                    LCD EMULATION FUNCTIONS
//  472  *
//  473  * Some evaluation boards are equipped with Liquid Crystal Displays
//  474  * (LCD) which may be used to display diagnostic information. These
//  475  * functions provide LCD emulation, sending the diagnostic strings
//  476  * to Z-Tool via the RS232 serial port. These functions are enabled
//  477  * when the "LCD_SUPPORTED" compiler flag is placed in the makefile.
//  478  *
//  479  * Most applications update both lines (1 and 2) of the LCD whenever
//  480  * text is posted to the device. This emulator assumes that line 1 is
//  481  * updated first (saved locally) and the formatting and send operation
//  482  * is triggered by receipt of line 2. Nothing will be transmitted if
//  483  * only line 1 is updated.
//  484  *
//  485  *************************************************************************************************/
//  486 
//  487 
//  488 /**************************************************************************************************
